    <!--
      Mesa 25.3.6, not the 24.3.0-devel revision the branch this was derived from pins.
      Android 17 compiles the guest with -std=gnu++23 and clang-r584948b's libc++, which
      declares std::unreachable() in <__utility/unreachable.h>. Mesa's src/util/macros.h
      defined a lowercase `unreachable` macro until 25.3.0, so the declaration expanded
      through the macro and every C++ translation unit that reaches <vector> failed with
      "error: expected unqualified-id". Mesa renamed the macro to UNREACHABLE in 25.3.0;
      25.3.6 is the current stable patch of that series. The revision below is the COMMIT the
      annotated tag mesa-25.3.6 points at, not the tag object, so it matches what
      `repo manifest -r` reports back.

      Verified drop-in from the device tree's point of view: android/Android.mk still gates
      on BOARD_MESA3D_USES_MESON_BUILD at the same line and still reads
      BOARD_MESA3D_GALLIUM_DRIVERS, which is the whole interface
      device/epam/aosp-xenvm-trout/xenvm_trout_arm64/BoardConfig.mk uses.

      One build-host requirement changes with it: mesa's meson floor moves 1.1.0 -> 1.4.0,
      and the Android build runs the HOST meson (android/mesa3d_cross.mk invokes it with
      PATH=/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin), so a host with meson older than 1.4.0 now fails at
      `meson setup`. Nothing else moves: the libdrm floor stays at 2.4.109 (AOSP 17 ships
      2.4.124), and Rust/bindgen remain unnecessary for this configuration, which builds
      only the virgl Gallium driver.
    -->
    <project path="vendor/epam/mesa3d_upstream" name="mesa/mesa" remote="fd" revision="06f9e28304d5d3f109c33535c1c25b9df5769af2"/> <!-- mesa-25.3.6 -->
